  "handoff": "# Typed PIPESTATUS six-probe reference preparation\n\nDate: 2026-08-29. AUTHOR READY for DIFFERENT preexecution review. **No actual native authority. P19–P24 all UNRUN; no expected outputs or semantic policy chosen.**\n\nExact root-supplied literals are in PROGRAMS.json and materialized/programs; six hashes/argv/env/empty-stdin bindings in COHORT/REQUESTS. P19 is exactly declare -p PIPESTATUS as first command, no prologue. No eval/source/profile/external command/variable-command/slash lookup/network/private path. Only fixed f invocations, builtin declarations/readonly/assignment/true/false and two finite pipelines. Zero fixtures and zero permitted effects.\n\nParent author5861ec9a8750de90bf38f93a2cd0df66198e8d9f; independent98192974514389759c96d20c7f35fe6050641c76; ROOTcf6c47b8a976bb71bd6dd419c103e23264e71a32 are retained references, not reused authority. SOURCE-AUTH.json binds selected stored parent blobs and fresh tool hashes. Three owner modules change (admission/entry/observation); six remain byte-identical. Old F05 effects permission is removed, all lookups forbidden, IDs/counts/profile/paths are separately versioned. Host FNPIPEOBS1 framing and raw byte preservation remain unchanged.\n\nDATA controls 12/12 PASS, 0 FAIL, 120 assertions. Three changed-module Node syntax children retired. No lifecycle fixture child, Bash, actual entry, native version, compiler/build/product/Worker or network ran. Bootstrap syntax/prepare/controls are the three controller images. All individual raw captures and failures, if any, are retained.\n\nExecutable preseal SHA256 ade56f23358e284df533f7e57e462ba927fb0386899061e90699977746424b6e; control result 72198874fe7144bbdbe45d75bd02311f0a4ba5869f46679a3d5995d13fdad7cc; exact prospective command string d4e97d0e932825d3c8318792b2c2d98bd4aa997800805f95bdfa1f091326140e. New runtime review/GO templates have strict finite fields and reject PENDING/non-numeric/old-profile authority. issued/expiry/latest-start UTC remain PENDING